# OS-SUITES-PARALLEL-1: suites that must run ONE AT A TIME, after the parallel set, because they share a host-wide resource (a lock, the process
# table, a fixed port, the installed ~/.claude). Format: <class>/<suite>, one per line, `#` comments. A suite not listed here runs in parallel
# (RUN_TESTS_JOBS, default 2). A new suite is parallel by default: add it here when it takes a lock, signals processes by pattern or binds a port.
ops-shell/single-instance
ops-shell/main-first
ops-shell/main-first-fairness
ops-shell/loop-watchdog
ops-shell/alert-wait
ops-shell/worktree-cleanup
ops-shell/wt-deps-prisma
ops-lib/disk-discipline
ops-lib/job-cadence
remediation/gate
